      "The Kookaburra closed at the end of 2025 and we took a hiatus, but Magic Monday\'s is coming back at <strong>The Starlight Cabaret</strong>, a new venue from the same ownership in Studio City. The space is lovely. Better sightlines, better production, same energy. If you love the Castle but want something more casual, no dress code, no membership, just show up in jeans and see excellent magic up close, this is your spot. It\'s going to be wonderful when we\'re back.",
      '<a href="https://www.blackrabbitrose.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Black Rabbit Rose</strong></a> in Hollywood. This is a <strong>Houston Brothers</strong> joint, the same people behind No Vacancy, Good Times at Davey Wayne\'s, Break Room 86. They know atmosphere better than almost anyone in this city and it shows. The cocktails are fantastic, the space feels like a modern speakeasy, and the magic is woven into the whole evening rather than being a separate "OK now watch the show" thing. They have rotating performers in an intimate theater space upstairs. Lovely date night. Lovely group outing. Just a cool place to be.',
      '<a href="https://www.thehollywoodroosevelt.com/events/los-angeles/magic-at-the-library-bar-11224649" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Magic at the Library Bar</strong></a> at <strong>The Hollywood Roosevelt</strong>. This one flies under the radar. Every Sunday evening, 6 to 8 PM, <strong>HUBB</strong> performs close-up magic in the Library Bar. HUBB is a veteran of both the Magic Castle and the Chicago Magic Lounge, and his sleight of hand is just... incredible. You sit there with a cocktail in one of the most beautiful hotel bars in Hollywood and watch impossible things happen three feet away. Tickets sell out. Book ahead.',
      '<a href="https://illusionmagiclounge.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Illusions Magic Lounge</strong></a> in Santa Monica. 150-seat theater with a rotating roster of magicians, comedians, and variety performers. Here\'s the thing I love about Illusions: you don\'t even need a ticket to experience magic there. The lounge area is open to walk-ins, and they have strolling magicians performing tableside while you have a drink. If you do grab a theater seat, every show feels personal. Great Westside option.',
      '<a href="https://www.marvynsmagictheater.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Marvyn\'s Magic Theater</strong></a> in La Quinta. OK technically this is out near Palm Springs, not LA. But I\'m including it because the caliber of talent they bring in rivals anything in the city. The desert setting adds something unexpected to the whole experience. Worth the drive if you\'re serious about seeing great magic. Trust me on that.',
      "Then there\'s the private magic scene, which most people don\'t even know exists. Some of the best magicians in LA perform exclusively at private events: mansion parties in Beverly Hills, corporate gatherings in the Hollywood Hills, intimate dinners in Malibu. None of it is advertised. It all runs on word of mouth and planner referrals. This is the world White Rabbit lives in. Creating one-of-a-kind experiences for hosts who want to give their guests something they\'ve never seen before.",
      "LA\'s magic scene is in a fantastic place right now. New venues keep popping up. The talent pool is deeper than it\'s ever been. And there\'s a growing audience of adults who get it, who understand that magic at its best is an art form, not a novelty act. Whether you\'re visiting the Castle for the first time, catching Magic Monday\'s in Studio City when we\'re back, or bringing White Rabbit to your next event, this city is where you fall in love with the impossible. I\'m biased. But I\'m also right.",
