      "What made Magic Monday's special from the beginning was its format: a curated lineup of top magicians and performers, rotating bi-monthly, in an intimate setting where every seat was a front-row seat. The show attracted some of the best talent in magic, comedy, and entertainment. Comedians like <strong>Adam Ray</strong>, <strong>Craig Robinson</strong>, <strong>Tiffany Haddish</strong>, and <strong>Dean Delray</strong> shared the stage with an incredible roster of magicians including <strong>Jackson Ridd</strong>, <strong>Nader Hanna</strong>, <strong>HUBB</strong>, <strong>Taylor Hughes</strong>, <strong>Kyle Marlett</strong>, <strong>Connor Mac</strong>, <strong>Michael Rayner</strong>, <strong>Franco Pascali</strong>, <strong>Day Mori</strong>, <strong>Jer Bear</strong>, <strong>Nelson Lee</strong>, <strong>Frankie Foti</strong>, <strong>Will Coile</strong>, <strong>Nick Paul</strong>, <strong>Blake Vogt</strong>, <strong>Alex Kazam</strong>, <strong>Miss Direction</strong>, <strong>Greg Van Holsbeck</strong>, <strong>Carlos Suarez</strong>, and <strong>David Stryker</strong>. <strong>Scott Syme</strong> hosted and performed throughout the run. From close-up card artists and mentalists to A-list comedians and variety performers, every show brought something unexpected. It was never the same show twice, and that unpredictability was part of the magic.",
